sentences.t:
Direvos de los cavalleros que levaron el menssaje;
al ora que lo sopo mio Çid el de Bivar,
plógol de coraçon e tornós a alegrar;
de la su boca conpeçó de fablar:

sentences.l:
I-will-tell-you of the knights who carried the message;
at-the hour that it learned my Çid him of Bivar,
it-pleased-him from heart and he-turned-himself to rejoice;
from the his mouth he-began of to-speak:

sentences.t:
E yo fincaré en Valençia, que mucho costadom ha;
grand locura seríe si la desenparás;
yo ffincaré en Valençia, ca la tengo por heredad.”

sentences.l:
And I shall-stay in Valençia, which much has-cost-me;
great folly it-would-be if it I-abandoned;
I shall-stay in Valençia, for it I-hold as inheritance.”

sentences.t:
Fabló Muño Gustioz, non speró a nadi:
“mio Çid vos saludava, e mandólo recabdar,
co[n] çiento cavalleros que privádol acorrades;

sentences.l:
Spoke Muño Gustioz, not he-waited for nobody:
“my Çid you was-greeting, and ordered-it to-see-to,
wi[th] a-hundred knights that quickly-him you-help;

sentences.t:
su mugier e sus fijas en Medina están;
que vayades por ellas, adugades gelas acá,
e ffata en Valençia dellas non vos partades.”

sentences.l:
his wife and his daughters in Medina are;
that you-go for them, you-bring them-to-him here,
and as-far-as in Valençia from-them not yourselves you-part.”

sentences.t:
Essa noch conducho les dio grand,
a la mañana pienssan de cavalgar;
çientol pidieron, mas él con dozientos va.

sentences.l:
That night provision to-them he-gave great,
at the morning they-think of to-ride;
a-hundred-of-him they-asked, but he with two-hundred goes.

sentences.t:
E en Medina todo el recabdo está;
vídolos venir armados temiós Minaya Alvar Fáñez,
envió dos cavalleros que sopiesse[n] la verdad;
esto non detarda[n], ca de coraçon lo han;

sentences.l:
And in Medina all the precaution is;
he-saw-them come armed, feared-himself Minaya Alvar Fáñez,
he-sent two knights that they-might-know[n] the truth;
this not they-delay[n], for of heart it they-have;

sentences.t:
e alcáyaz Ave[n]galvón con su[e]s fuerças que trahe,
por sabor de mio Çid de grand óndral dar;
todos vienen en uno, agora llegarán.”

sentences.l:
and alcaide Ave[n]galvón with hi[e]s forces which he-brings,
for pleasure of my Çid of great honor-to-him to-give;
all come in one, now they-will-arrive.”

sentences.t:
Los que ivan mesurando e llegando delant
luego toman armas e tómanse a deportar;
por çerca de Salón tan grandes gozos van.

sentences.l:
Those who were-going scouting and arriving ahead
at-once take arms and take-themselves to disport;
by near of Salón so great joys they-go.

sentences.t:
“Tan buen día convusco, Minaya Albar Fáñez!
Traedes estas dueñas por o valdremos más,
mugier del Çid lidiador e sus ffijas naturales;

sentences.l:
“So good day with-you, Minaya Albar Fáñez!
You-bring these ladies through which we-shall-be-worth more,
wife of-the Çid fighter and his daughters natural;
